    <DataNode elementId="AT1G43670-MONOMER" textLabel="fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9MA79" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="515" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, dreher">|FRAME: AT1G43670-MONOMER FINS1| is a fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase based on enzymatic assays performed on |FRAME: ORG-5993 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt; col| protoplasts overexpressing |FRAME: AT1G43670-MONOMER FINS1|. Mutation of two conserved serine residues (S126A, S127A) abolishes the enzyme&apos;s catalytic activity. Unlike its chloroplastic counterpart |FRAME: AT3G54050-MONOMER cpFBP|, |FRAME: AT1G43670-MONOMER FINS1| likely plays a role in |FRAME: SUCROSE sucrose| cytosolic metabolism in the light |CITS: [21253566]|. Therefore, it is not surprising that &lt;i&gt;fins1&lt;/i&gt; mutants have reduced levels of |FRAME: SUCROSE sucrose| and have elevated levels of |FRAME: Starch starch| during the day |CITS: [10998187]|. This enzyme, in addition to catalyzing the formation of |FRAME: FRUCTOSE-6P D-fructose-6-phosphate|, appears to play a role in fructose-mediated signaling that is independent of its enzymatic activity |CITS: [21253566]|. In addition, atcfbp-1 mutants have reduced photosynthetic rates |CITS: [18811733]|. Although |FRAME: AT1G43670-MONOMER FINS1| is expected to be cytosolic, a GFP-tagged version localizes to the cytoplasm and the nucleus. It is unclear whether its signaling function depends on its nuclear localization |CITS: [21253566]|. FBPase enzymes typically exist as homotetrameric complexes |CITS: [1849642]|, but this has not yet been experiementally verified for |FRAME: AT1G43670-MONOMER FINS1|. In addition, these enzymes are typically subject to allosteric inhibition by |FRAME: CPD-535 &amp;beta;-D-fructose 2,6-bisphosphate| and |FRAME: AMP AMP| |CITS:[CSEKE84]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G43670-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G43670.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR11556" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="Q9MA79" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prints" value="PR00115" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="Q9MA79" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR033391" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF00316" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Phylomedb" value="Q9MA79" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Prosite" value="PS00124" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9MA79" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="cytosolic fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-18716" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G43670.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G43670" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_21253566" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_10998187" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_18811733" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_1849642" />
    </DataNode>
